        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Beautifully Presented Four-Bedroom Home with Dublin Mountain Views\r\n\r\nA rare opportunity to acquire an outstanding family home in superb condition, enjoying beautiful views of the Dublin Mountains and a private, non-overlooked setting.\r\n\r\nLovingly maintained and thoughtfully upgraded by its owners over the past 21 years, this impressive property offers bright, versatile accommodation, quality finishes and exceptional storage throughout. Highlights include an open-plan kitchen and dining room, a beautifully refurbished sitting room, four bedrooms, an impressive attic conversion and meticulously landscaped gardens.\r\n\r\nThe home is presented in turnkey condition, allowing the new owners to move in and enjoy it immediately.\r\n\r\nGround floor\r\nThe welcoming entrance hall features tiled flooring, elegant wall panelling and cleverly designed custom-built understairs storage.\r\nAt the heart of the home is the bright open-plan kitchen and dining room. Tiled throughout, it features a timeless Shaker-style kitchen complemented by solid oak worktops and generous space for family dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe elegant sitting room has recently refurbished solid oak flooring, contemporary coving and a striking solid marble fireplace, creating an inviting space in which to relax.\r\n\r\nA stylishly upgraded guest WC, with tiled finishes and a modern toilet and wash-hand basin, completes the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nFirst floor\r\nThe main bedroom benefits from custom-built wardrobes and a private ensuite with a Triton T90 electric shower.\r\nThree further versatile rooms all feature solid oak flooring and custom-made wardrobes. These can be used as additional bedrooms, a home office, nursery or dressing room, depending on the purchaser's needs.\r\n\r\nThe upgraded main bathroom is fully tiled and includes a bath, power shower, modern WC and wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nAttic conversion\r\nA particular feature is the large attic conversion, which provides valuable additional space. Bright and versatile, it is ideally suited to use as a home office, second sitting room, hobby room, playroom or occasional guest accommodation, subject to the relevant planning and building regulations.\r\n\r\nGardens and parking\r\nThe beautifully maintained rear garden offers a peaceful and private outdoor retreat. It features mature planting, a patio area ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining, and a useful garden shed with an electricity supply.\r\n\r\nTo the front, an attractive landscaped flower bed and granite-style cobble-lock driveway create excellent kerb appeal. The driveway provides off-street parking for up to three cars.\r\n\r\nWith its enviable outlook, excellent condition, adaptable living space and beautifully maintained gardens, this is a distinctive family home that deserves early viewing."
      },
